00:01:29.963 --> 00:01:31.490
So I'm excited to learn about photography.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:32.323
Tell me a little about yourself.

00:01:32.323 --> 00:01:34.820
- I'm Jason Risorto, I'm
a Brooklyn based landscape

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:35.960
and cityscape photographer.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.100
My images are known for being

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.835
bright sunrises and sunsets

00:01:39.835 --> 00:01:41.770
with Manhattan as the backdrop,

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:43.550
and I also like to really incorporate

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:45.280
foreground and midground elements

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.420
to make it more of a
landscape type of photo

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:49.680
as opposed to just a
typical New York City shot.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.000
So let's go down to the waterfront.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.140
We're gonna take a few photos

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:53.110
and I'm gonna give you some tips

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.165
and hopefully we'll get something great.

00:01:55.165 --> 00:01:57.748
(upbeat music)

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.840
- [Kyle] So we spent all afternoon

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:07.738
wandering around Brooklyn
and taking photos.

00:02:07.738 --> 00:02:11.060
Jason gave me lots of tips on
how to improve my photography

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.110
and talked to me about
his approach to Instagram.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.160
We finished the day off
taking a sunset photo

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:17.793
of downtown Manhattan before heading home.

00:02:17.793 --> 00:02:20.376
(upbeat music)

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.500
Before me and Jason
split up the other day,

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.240
he gave me three challenges to complete.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:32.350
One of them is to recreate
three famous Instagram photos

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:33.970
so I'm gonna do one at
the Brooklyn Bridge,

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:34.980
one at the Manhattan Bridge,

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.100
and one at the top of The Rock.

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.880
Number two, incorporate a
friend into one of my photos,

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.630
and finally three, wake up for sunrise.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:44.440
If I can get anything
close to what Jason does,

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:45.750
I would be so psyched.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:46.910
Today, it's not looking great.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:49.240
It's really cloudy out, but I'm here,

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:50.963
so gonna take the photos anyways.

00:02:54.659 --> 00:02:56.360
Right next to the
Brooklyn Bridge is another

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.010
very popular Instagram spot.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.533
It's the Manhattan Bridge,
this blue one right down here.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.350
So recreation number two also

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.900
kind of a failure, unfortunately.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:07.620
I mean, there was a 100 people over there

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.790
taking Instagrams, engagement photos,

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.750
pregnancy photos, it's just way too busy

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:12.930
to get a shot right now.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:14.870
For the third recreation,
I'm gonna head back

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.590
to Manhattan and go to the top

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:17.843
of Rockefeller Center.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.970
Okay, so update on Rockefeller Center.

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:29.250
I went there and it was
a two hour wait to get in

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.205
and it cost $35.

00:03:31.205 --> 00:03:33.080
I don't have $35 to take a picture.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:34.770
Yeah, I didn't get any good photos today.

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:36.506
Day one's off to not a
great start on my own.

00:03:36.506 --> 00:03:39.470
Hoping that tomorrow, when
I put someone in my photo,

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:40.600
that'll be good, and then hopefully

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:42.500
when I do my early morning photo,

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:45.150
I'll get some really
interesting light, so we'll see.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:48.070
- I'm prepared for the
picture, let's do it.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:49.820
I'm scared, I have to do a handstand.

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:52.000
I should do it shirtless,
probably, shouldn't I?

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.790
- So Eric decided to take it up a notch

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:54.900
and take his shirt off for the Instagram.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.803
We're going for the one
handed handstand right now.

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:58.220
- This is for Kyle, I just care

00:03:58.220 --> 00:03:59.560
about Kyle getting views.

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:00.854
I'll do whatever for Kyle.

00:04:00.854 --> 00:04:03.630
- All right, let's make it happen.

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:05.980
So I think we got the
photo, it looks pretty cool.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:07.480
Eric did a handstand, but he accidentally

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.460
did it in glass.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:09.870
- Yeah, I'm not flipping you guys off.

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:12.398
I, I'm bleeding, I got glass in my finger.

00:04:12.398 --> 00:04:15.300
So I'm gonna go, I have to go get it out.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.250
- We got the picture though,

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:17.430
so I mean, that's what matters right?

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:18.383
- [Eric] Wow, Kyle.

00:04:19.471 --> 00:04:21.111
(alarm rings)

00:04:21.111 --> 00:04:21.944
- Oh God.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:23.743
I'm up.

00:04:23.743 --> 00:04:25.850
I'm just gonna pack up
and head to New Jersey.

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:27.090
Okay, good morning.

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:29.960
So I am up and out of
the house before 5:00 AM.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:31.840
And so far, I'm not liking it.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:33.600
It's dark and it's kind of cold,

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.600
and there's no one around.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.283
Gonna go take my picture now.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:41.360
All right, so one hour later,

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:43.470
I made it out here to
Morris Canal State Park

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.970
in New Jersey, I have an
awesome view of the city.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:47.800
I'm just waiting for the sun to come up.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.321
I'm excited, it's freezing out,

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:52.716
but I'm definitely awake
now, so that's good.

00:04:52.716 --> 00:04:55.023
Just waiting patiently, so.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:00.150
The sun is slowly starting to rise.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:03.970
It is getting way colder by the second

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.527
right on the water, so

00:05:05.527 --> 00:05:07.819
the wind is whipping at my face right now.

00:05:07.819 --> 00:05:10.763
Hands are freezing, I forgot gloves today.

00:05:11.987 --> 00:05:13.183
♪ See your outline in the dark ♪

00:05:13.183 --> 00:05:15.063
♪ And hear the blood run in your heart ♪

00:05:15.063 --> 00:05:17.230
♪ When we're in each other's ♪

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:18.690
So update, the pictures are
looking better by the second.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:20.624
This is actually, this is really cool.

00:05:20.624 --> 00:05:22.840
And it's actually really
peaceful out here.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:25.420
I never do this, just
come out in the morning,

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:28.826
no music or anything, just
kind of hanging out by myself.

00:05:28.826 --> 00:05:31.096
And there's some geese over there.

00:05:31.096 --> 00:05:33.630
I'm still waiting for the sky to kind of

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:35.180
light up the way I'm hoping it will.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.490
To make the photos more
interesting for now,

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:37.960
I'm gonna put myself in it.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.123
Coming out onto the rocks and pose.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:45.956
The sky is starting to look
really nice, so that's exciting.

00:05:45.956 --> 00:05:48.765
It's getting more and more red back there.

00:05:48.765 --> 00:05:52.105
All right, it literally keeps
getting better by the second.

00:05:52.105 --> 00:05:54.563
Look at that.

00:05:56.860 --> 00:05:58.383
All right, that's pretty
much it for sunrise.

00:05:58.383 --> 00:06:00.530
I mean, I was really
hesitant about waking up

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:01.980
and coming out here, but

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:02.813
I've had a great morning,

00:06:02.813 --> 00:06:04.410
I think this is really nice, actually.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:08.430
All right, so is it the best
Instagram of New York City?

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.750
I mean, probably not, but
I think it's pretty good.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:13.270
And Jason even commented Nice, man.

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:15.118
With that emoji, so.

00:06:15.118 --> 00:06:17.950
If you're still watching, I
assume you like photography,

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.990
so I will tell you a few
things that Jason told me.

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:21.610
One is really plan your shot out.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.340
He told me to get to whatever
destination I'm headed to

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:27.010
20 to 30 minutes before
it's actually time to shoot.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:28.740
So number two is definitely
check the weather,

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.910
so to get those really
beautiful colors in the sky,

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:32.590
you actually need to
have some cloud coverage.

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:34.320
Not a whole lot, you wanna
make sure there's a gap

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:36.300
in the horizon, so the
sunlight can come through

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:37.480
and bounce off those clouds,

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:40.240
and number three is you don't
need a really crazy camera

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:43.920
to get photos, it's all about
timing, light and composition.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.160
And I think that's it.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:47.040
Hopefully, the next
photo that I try to take,

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:49.507
I don't need to wake up
at 4:00 AM to get it.

